# Theme versioning (SemVer X.Y.Z)

Source of truth: repo-root `VERSION` (line 1 = `X.Y.Z`, line 2 = kebab-case slug). Shopify `theme_version` must match line 1.

Current line: **11.0.0** (`nine-page-redesign`). 10.1.0 = manufacturing-and-landing-cart. 10.0.0 = numa-storefront. V9 / V9.1 / V9.2 = 9.0.0 / 9.1.0 / 9.2.0. 9.3.0 = storefront-polish-review. 9.4.0 = landing-pages-and-gtm.

## Export name

`Valtora-Shopify-Theme-X.Y.Z-<slug>.zip`

- Slug: 2–5 kebab-case words for **what changed**, not “update” or “fixes”
- Folder: `checkpoints/X.Y.Z-<slug>/`
- Same basename in Downloads
- Zip root = `valtora-theme/` contents (not a nested folder)
- Checkpoint README = the full release notes

Example: `Valtora-Shopify-Theme-9.2.0-order-status-app-proxy.zip`

## When the user asks for an export

Bump `VERSION`, write a new slug, then package.

| What changed since last export | Bump |
|---|---|
| Fixes, copy tweaks, packaging only | **PATCH** — `9.2.0` → `9.2.1` |
| New feature or page behaviour | **MINOR** — `9.2.0` → `9.3.0` (reset patch to 0) |

Never bump **MAJOR** on a routine export.

## When the user asks to save a version

They are happy with it. Bump **MAJOR** and reset: `9.3.1` → **`10.0.0`**. New slug for that freeze. That is the kept milestone.

## Do not

- Re-export or bump unless they asked
- Reuse `V9` / `V9.1` style names after `9.2.0`
- Ship a zip whose name is only the version number
